(6196828, 915385, 96751, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your first entry!  The use of tilt is a good one, the low pov and dof are excellent, and the motion blur of the bow is fantastic, although I find the greenish/yellow overall cast a bit unattractive.  I hope this does well for you.  <br/> <br/>It will be interesting to see how you achieved the floating notes within advanced editing rules (hanging from strings would be my guess).  However, if you inserted them as graphics after taking the image, don''t be surprised (or disappointed) if you get DQ''d.  All the best photographers on DPC have at least one DQ under their belt.  Even the ribbon-winners.</td>', 'Congrats on your first entry!  The use of tilt is a good one, the low pov and dof are excellent, and the motion blur of the bow is fantastic, although I find the greenish/yellow overall cast a bit unattractive.  I hope this does well for you.   It will be interesting to see how you achieved the floating notes within advanced editing rules (hanging from strings would be my guess).  However, if you inserted them as graphics after taking the image, don''t be surprised (or disappointed) if you get DQ''d.  All the best photographers on DPC have at least one DQ under their belt.  Even the ribbon-winners.', '2010-10-20 13:32:53.000000', NULL, 1),
