(6230031, 915417, 68504, '<td valign="top">Yawn or woof?  Never before seen suck down whirlpooling of the tongue. Fab view.</td>', 'Yawn or woof?  Never before seen suck down whirlpooling of the tongue. Fab view.', '2010-11-22 13:37:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(6230064, 915417, 87751, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tnun:</b></div><hr/><i> Yawn or woof?  Never before seen suck down whirlpooling of the tongue. Fab view. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Definitely not a yawn...or at least not the kind that indicates fatigue.  It was more of a Border Collie roar, which I imagine was part stress and part arousal.  This dog competes in agility and was watching other (very fast and high drive) dogs doing the same at an agility competition.  Thanks for all the comments.</td>', 'Originally posted by tnun: Yawn or woof?  Never before seen suck down whirlpooling of the tongue. Fab view.   Definitely not a yawn...or at least not the kind that indicates fatigue.  It was more of a Border Collie roar, which I imagine was part stress and part arousal.  This dog competes in agility and was watching other (very fast and high drive) dogs doing the same at an agility competition.  Thanks for all the comments.', '2010-11-22 13:54:25.000000', NULL, 0),
